# Operators defined among the painters that do not paint.
#
# tests/check-painting-operators.sh reads the painting operators off the
# files that define them and holds them to the cross-product in
# tests/device_features_test.ps. An operator listed here is one that
# lives in those files without marking a page, and the reason it does
# not is written beside it. A line here for an operator no file defines
# fails, so an exemption cannot outlive what it was written about.

# The hit-testing family (PLRM 8.2 infill and its five siblings). Each
# asks whether a point or a rectangle would be covered if the path were
# painted, and answers a boolean: the question is about the path and the
# clip, and the device is never handed a mark. They sit in
# data/paint.ps because they answer it by the same machinery a fill
# resolves its spans with, which is what makes the answer agree with
# what a fill would do.
infill
ineofill
instroke
inufill
inueofill
inustroke
